<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hadım Suleiman Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hadım Suleiman Pasha was an Ottoman commander and governor of Rumelia under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a>. In January 1475 he led a large Ottoman army into Moldavia and was decisively defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-the-great">Stephen the Great</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vaslui">Battle of Vaslui</a>. The defeat was among the heaviest suffered by Ottoman arms in that century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hadim-suleiman-pasha.jpg" alt="Hadım Suleiman Pasha" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Theodor de Bry · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arolsen_Klebeband_01_465_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
